# Salesforce Schema Drift Process

## Problem Statement
- Reports contained missing or outdated information
- Reports were not maintained and quality was not ensured
- Program staff submitted ~10-15 tickets per month on issues with reports
  related to changes in the Salesforce environment
- ~30-40 hours of staff capacity wasted on investigating the issues with
  the reports and making necessary updates to correc the changes

## My Role
I was the lead project manager for the initiative. I procured the project plan, gathered
requirements, designed the process, documented and trained staff and provided
hypercare as I transitioned ownership of the process to the data analytics team.

## Stack
- Salesforce: Report and dashboard schema drift process
- LucidChart and LucidSpark: Discovery and process documentation 
- Asana: Project timeline, task assignment, and project updates

## Approach
1. **Gathered Requirements** - led discovery meetings with our Salesforce Adminstrators
and data analytics teams to determine prioritized needs and uncover technical pain points.
2. **Discover and Refine Process** - brainstormed, drafted and finetuned the process to ensure 
Salesforce changes are communicated and reports and dashboards are maintained.
3. **Documented and Trained** - Drafted material and trained staff in several workshops on 
the new process to foster adoption and establish the formal process.
4. **Hypercare and Feedback** - Provided follow up training and gathered feedback on the new
process to learn and continuously improve post project. 

## Key Artifacts
- Add: Kick off deck with project plan
- Add: WBS (Work Breakdown Structure)
- Add: Post project objective metrics / stats

# Solution
Data Analysts alerted of Salesforce changes and recieve reports on relevant changes that 
require reporting and dashboard maintenance. The project implemented a bi-weekly touchpoint 
between Salesforce Administrators and the Data Analytics team to encourage cross team 
collaboration and enable both teams to understand the downstream effects of Salesforce updates.

## Endorsement & Evidence
Four months post process implementation, Salesforce Administrators reported finding the
the collaboration with the Data Analytics team helpful and informative on the effect of
their work. Data Analysts noticed a decrease in support tickets on report discrepancies.
